@startuml
title mp-dance-lora — Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Performer" as Performer
actor "VJ Operator" as Operator
actor "Researcher / Model Trainer" as Researcher

rectangle "mp-dance-lora Dance VJ System" {
  usecase "Capture live movement" as UC1
  usecase "Estimate body pose" as UC2
  usecase "Project visuals in real time" as UC3
  usecase "Continue motion when performer is still" as UC4
  usecase "Calibrate camera and projection" as UC5
  usecase "Adjust effects and motion parameters" as UC6
  usecase "Record timestamped pose data" as UC7
  usecase "Export pose dataset (JSONL)" as UC8
  usecase "Analyze motion quality and timing" as UC9
  usecase "Train candidate motion / LoRA model" as UC10
  usecase "Evaluate candidate model" as UC11
  usecase "Promote or roll back model version" as UC12
  usecase "Monitor latency, FPS and memory" as UC13
}

Performer --> UC1
Performer --> UC3
Operator --> UC3
Operator --> UC5
Operator --> UC6
Operator --> UC13
Researcher --> UC8
Researcher --> UC9
Researcher --> UC10
Researcher --> UC11
Researcher --> UC12

UC1 .> UC2 : <<include>>
UC2 .> UC3 : <<include>>
UC3 .> UC4 : <<extend>>\n[no reliable live movement]
UC1 .> UC7 : <<include>>
UC7 .> UC8 : <<include>>
UC8 .> UC9 : <<include>>
UC9 .> UC10 : <<include>>
UC10 .> UC11 : <<include>>
UC11 .> UC12 : <<include>>

note bottom of UC12
Model updates are validated offline/background.
Promote at a safe motion boundary; retain rollback.
Training never blocks live projection.
end note
@enduml
